      "content": "but that's just what people say when they don't see what's right in front of them. it's way too specific to just be \"pattern seeking.\" like, the blue butterfly and the yellow raincoat... those colors are so bright and distinct. and the timing with the 7:12 am thing? \n\nif you look at it from a mathematical or probability perspective, isn't it possible that these aren't just random, but are actually part of a stochastic sequence? if i told you these events were part of a larger data set that actually follows a certain frequency, would you still call it just \"brain forcing meaning\"? i feel like you're dismissing the data because it doesn't fit a standard causal model, but there's definitely a logic to it if you look deeper.",
